###################################################################################################
# PROFANITY FILTER DICTIONARY
#
#    Served to clients over plain HTTP by this worldserver (enable with
#    ProfanityFilter.ServeURL in worldserver.conf) and applied by the CLIENT itself - the same
#    dictionary retail downloads from the depot. When enabled, the worldserver builds this file
#    into the blob format the client expects and publishes it; the file is re-read at every
#    worldserver startup, and every edit changes the published content hash, so clients
#    re-download instead of using their cached copy.
#
#    Format:
#      - A [section] header names the dictionary type for the lines below it. The client looks
#        up "bad" for the recruitment-description sanitizer; retail also ships "reserved" and
#        "hatespeech".
#      - One regular expression per line, in the client's own regex dialect (case-insensitive;
#        word boundaries with \b are supported).
#      - Empty lines are skipped; '#' starts a comment.
#
#    NOTE: keep at least one [bad] entry - with an empty "bad" dictionary the client wipes
#    every recruitment description instead of checking it. To disable filtering entirely, keep
#    a single never-matching placeholder expression instead of removing the section.
#
#    The worldserver reads the working copy from "<DataDir>/profanity_filters.conf" (copy this
#    template there, or let the worldserver create it on first run - it seeds the same retail
#    ruRU list this template carries).
###################################################################################################

